+//! `wyrd s3 --chunk-size N` is honoured end to end (#738), driven through the BUILT `wyrd`
+//! binary — not `serve_s3_role` — so the test references no symbol the fix adds and the
+//! pre-fix tree compiles it and fails on the assertion. Pre-fix, `ParsedArgs::parse` records
+//! an unknown `--chunk-size` and nobody reads it, so the role starts, ignores the flag, and
+//! chunks at the 1 MiB default.
+//!
+//! * With `--chunk-size N`, one object of `4N` bytes PUT through the role lands as exactly
+//!   four chunk directories under `<data-dir>/chunks` (`FsChunkStore` files each chunk as a
+//!   `<32-hex>` directory of `<index>.frag` fragments).
+//! * With NO `--chunk-size`, the identical object lands as the chunk count 1 MiB implies —
+//!   absence selects the shared `DEFAULT_CHUNK_SIZE`, unchanged from today.
+//! * `0` and `1073741825` (one past the inclusive 1 GiB ceiling) exit non-zero, naming the
+//!   flag, without the role ever printing its listen line; `1` and `1073741824` start. A
+//!   non-numeric value and a signed one are refused the same way, and the `wyrd s3` usage
+//!   line lists the flag.
+//! * Over the CLUSTER composition (`--endpoints`, fragments over gRPC to a production D
+//!   server), a 32 MiB chunk — whose RS(6,3) fragments exceed tonic's 4 MiB default message
+//!   limit — PUTs, lands as ONE chunk on the D server, and GETs back byte-identical: an
+//!   accepted chunk size is one the cluster transport can carry.
+//!
+//! Every role is pinned to the local `redb` + `mem` composition with explicit flags, so a
+//! developer environment exporting `WYRD_METADATA_BACKEND` / `WYRD_COORDINATION_BACKEND`
+//! cannot redirect it. Every child is killed by a drop guard on every exit path (the role
+//! blocks forever), and every wait is bounded, so a pre-fix binary that wrongly starts is a
+//! red, never a hang.
+
+#![forbid(unsafe_code)]
+
+use std::io::{BufRead, BufReader, Read, Write};
+use std::net::{SocketAddr, TcpStream};
+use std::path::Path;
+use std::process::{Child, Command, ExitStatus, Stdio};
+use std::sync::mpsc::{self, Receiver, RecvTimeoutError};
+use std::sync::Arc;
+use std::time::{Duration, Instant};
+
+use wyrd_chunkstore_fs::FsChunkStore;
+use wyrd_coordination_mem::MemCoordination;
